# Dev Environment Sync

Ansible playbooks to sync a standardized development environment across remote servers and configure local machine settings.

## Structure

Each tool gets its own subdirectory under `playbooks/` with a `sync.yml` entry point and a `templates/` directory for any Jinja2 templates.

## Setup

### 1. Install Ansible

```bash
python3 -m pip install --user pipx
pipx install --include-deps ansible
```

### 2. Configure vault password

Generate a random password and write it to `.vault_pass`:

```bash
openssl rand -base64 32 > .vault_pass
chmod 600 .vault_pass
```

`.vault_pass` is gitignored. Never commit it.

## Usage

Run all playbooks:
```bash
./run-all-playbooks.sh
```

Run against a specific server:
```bash
./run-all-playbooks.sh --limit host1
```

Run a single playbook:
```bash
ansible-playbook playbooks/bash/sync.yml
ansible-playbook playbooks/ssh/sync.yml
```

Run a single playbook targeting a group or host:
```bash
ansible-playbook playbooks/<tool>/sync.yml -l <group or host>
```


Dry run (preview changes without applying):
```bash
./run-all-playbooks.sh --check --diff
```

## Secrets

Secrets and sensitive variables can be encrypted with Ansible Vault (AES-256) and stored in `group_vars/**/vault.yml`. You can create a plaintext file named `.vault_pass` that contains your vault password and pass this into ansible-vault so you don't have to type in the vault password every time.


NOTE: It is recommended to save your `.vault_pass` (NOT in git)

### Create a new vault file

```bash
ansible-vault create group_vars/all/vault.yml --vault-password-file .vault_pass
```

Or encrypt an existing plaintext file:

```bash
ansible-vault encrypt group_vars/all/vault.yml --vault-password-file .vault_pass
```

### Edit an existing vault file

```bash
ansible-vault edit group_vars/all/vault.yml --vault-password-file .vault_pass 
```

### View a vault file without editing

```bash
ansible-vault view group_vars/all/vault.yml --vault-password-file .vault_pass
```

> **Pro-tip:** You don't have to write `--vault-password-file .vault_pass` as long as [ansible.cfg](./ansible.cfg) has `.vault_password_file = .vault_pass`. In this repo, this should be the case.